## Why This Is Asked
Tests design for multi-tenant ML services with SLA adherence, privacy, and drift handling in a single-region, VPC-bound setup.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoints; per-tenant routing; fair-share scheduling
- QoS, concurrency, canary rollouts; drift detection and retraining cadence
- Data locality, PrivateLink, encryption, audit logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode showing tenant routing
function route(request){
  const tenant = request.tenantId;
  const model = loadTenantModelIfNeeded(tenant);
  return model.predict(request.features);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to integrate explainability, bias auditing, drift monitoring, and controlled deployment in a multi-tenant, VPC-isolated AWS environment.

## Key Concepts

- SageMaker Clarify for bias and explainability
- Model Monitor drift detection
- PrivateLink and private feature store integration
- Canary rollout with per-tenant isolation
- Auditable logging to S3

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing snippet for multi-tenant endpoint
function routeTenant(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const endpoint = `rt-endpoint-${tenant}`;
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, req.body);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce data leakage prevention across tenants?
- How would you scale explainability reporting for thousands of tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical, production-ready approach to multi-tenant inference, with per-tenant routing, canary risk controls, and drift/latency monitoring within a VPC-bound data-residency model.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Endpoint variants and traffic weighting
- Per-tenant routing and isolation
- PrivateLink data lake access
- Canary rollout and rollback triggers
- Drift and latency monitoring, autoscaling, and cost control

## Code Example
